   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public service law, in relation to filing gas safety\nreports",
    "basePrintNo": "S1380",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1380-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §66-q, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1380\n\nSPONSOR: BROOKS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to filing gas safety\nreports\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to increase gas safety and promote public\ninterest\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. amends the public service law by adding a new section 66-p to\nprovide annual gas safety reports to be filed by each gas corporation.\nEach report shall include a description of, strategic planning and deci-\nsion making methodology used to determine the prioritization of pipeline\nreplacement projects, the corporations operation and maintenance activ-\nities related to gas safety, the corporations inspections of its intra-\nstate transmission and distribution lines, and any other information\nthat the department may require. The report shall also include a list of\npipeline replacement projects completed in the last year by the compa-\nny's employees and a list of the same projects completed by contractors.\nIf there is not a substantial change in a gas corporations report since\nthe most recently filed report, the corporation may file an updated\nreport. If a report is found to be deficient, the commission may request\nreasonable improvements to such report.\n\nSection 2. is the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill would require gas corporations to produce an annual gas safety\nreport for the purposes of increasing transparency, accountability, and\npublic safety. Natural gas must be used and delivered in the safest\npossible manner. An annual gas safety report by each gas corporation\nwill be an additional tool for the public, the Public Service Commis-\nsion, and the Legislature to ensure that every possible effort is being\nmade to ensure the safe delivery and use of natural gas.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
